#### Product FAQs

- **What exactly does Altaeron™ do?** Altaeron uses a dial-controlled tension system and structured hinge to apply adjustable support around the big toe. It is designed to guide the toe toward a straighter position and help address crowding around the bunion.

- **Will I feel it working immediately?** You should feel the device applying tension during your first properly adjusted session.

- **Does Altaeron straighten the big toe?** Altaeron is designed to guide the big toe toward a straighter position while you wear it. How much lasting alignment change occurs depends on your bunion severity, joint flexibility, and consistency of use.

- **How quickly can I notice relief?** Some users report a difference during their first sessions, while others need more time. Your experience may depend on the source and severity of your discomfort.

- **How long until I see alignment changes?** The toe can appear straighter while the device is applying tension. More lasting changes may develop with consistent use over time. The degree and timing of improvement depend on bunion severity and joint flexibility.

- **Can Altaeron™ make my bunion look smaller?** Yes — improving the position of the big toe can help make the bunion area look less prominent. With consistent use, you may notice a straighter-looking toe, less crowding, and a visible improvement in the appearance of your bunion. The amount of change depends on the severity and flexibility of your bunion.

- **Can Altaeron™ reverse a bunion?** For people with mild to moderate, flexible bunions, improving toe positioning may be possible with consistent corrective support and appropriate foot care. Altaeron is designed to help guide the big toe toward a straighter position, reduce crowding, and improve the appearance of the bunion area over time. The degree of improvement depends on how flexible the joint is and how advanced the bunion has become.

- **Can Altaeron™ help prevent my bunion from getting worse?** Altaeron is designed to counter the inward drift of the big toe and support better alignment. By making toe positioning part of your regular foot-care routine, you can take a proactive approach to managing your bunion and helping limit further progression. Results depend on the severity of the bunion, joint flexibility, and consistency of use.

- **Why not just use a toe spacer?** A basic toe spacer generally separates the toes passively. Altaeron uses an adjustable tension mechanism, allowing you to control the level of pull rather than relying only on a fixed spacer.

- **Why does adjustable tension matter?** A fixed level of stretch may feel too strong at first or too mild as you adapt. The dial lets you make gradual adjustments to find a setting that feels firm but comfortable.

- **How long should I wear it?** Start with shorter sessions and gradually build toward approximately 20–30 minutes at a time, following the product instructions and your comfort level. Consistency matters more than forcing longer sessions.

- **Should correction hurt?** No. You should feel a firm stretch, not sharp pain. Reduce the tension or remove the device if you experience sharp pain, numbness, tingling, or significant irritation.

- **Should I combine Altaeron with exercises?** Foot-strengthening exercises and suitable footwear may complement a conservative bunion-care routine. If you have significant pain or a more advanced deformity, ask a qualified healthcare professional which exercises are appropriate.

- **Can I walk while wearing it?** Altaeron is best suited to seated or resting sessions, especially when using stronger tension. Avoid walking in it unless the product instructions specifically confirm that it is safe to do so.

- **Who has the greatest potential for improvement?** People with mild to moderate bunions and a big toe that remains relatively flexible may have more potential to improve positioning through conservative care. Results depend on individual circumstances.

- **Does Altaeron fit both left and right feet?** Yes. The adjustable design can be used on either the left or right foot, one foot at a time.

- **Will it fit my foot?** The adjustable straps are designed to accommodate a wide range of adult foot sizes. Check the product dimensions and fit instructions before ordering.

- **Can I wear Altaeron inside shoes?** The structured frame and dial add bulk, so it may not fit comfortably inside every shoe. At-home sessions are generally the more suitable use.

- **What comes with one order?** Each unit includes one Altaeron™ Adjustable Bunion Corrector. It can be used on either the left or right foot, one foot at a time.

- **What are the product specifications?** Approx. size: 3.94 × 3.15 × 0.98 in (10 × 8 × 2.5 cm) Fit: Adjustable for adult feet Frame: ABS support structure Padding: Soft fabric and silicone contact areas Adjustment: Dial-controlled steel-wire tension system Hinge: Rotating design

