#### Product FAQs

- **What does the dial actually do?** The dial adjusts the tension around the brace, letting you fine-tune how secure and supportive it feels around your knee.

- **Do I need the Left or Right version?** Choose the side that matches the knee you plan to wear it on. DialFit has separate Left Knee and Right Knee versions.

- **How do I choose my size?** Use the Size Guide and choose according to the manufacturer's body-weight range.

- **Can I use it for walking, stairs or workouts?** Yes. DialFit is designed for active movement such as walking, stairs, gym training, running, hiking and everyday activities.

- **Can I wear it during a long work shift?** Yes. The adjustable design is useful for people who spend long periods standing or walking, including nurses, teachers, retail workers, hospitality staff and other on-your-feet jobs. You can adjust the tension as your comfort needs change throughout the day.

- **How tight should I wear it?** DialFit should feel snug and supportive, not painfully tight. If you experience numbness, tingling, unusual swelling or discomfort, loosen or remove it.

- **Is it bulky?** No. DialFit uses a lightweight stretch construction designed to provide support without the bulk of many traditional rigid knee braces.

- **What if I have arthritis, stiffness or an existing knee problem?** For knees that feel stiff, achy or less confident during walking, stairs or everyday movement, DialFit provides adjustable external support that can help the knee feel more secure while worn. It is not intended to diagnose, cure or repair an underlying joint condition or injury.

- **What if I also have varicose veins or heavy legs?** DialFit is designed for knee support rather than vein treatment. People who spend long periods standing or walking — including those who also experience tired or heavy legs — may use it for additional knee-focused support during the day.

- **Who is DialFit designed for?** DialFit is designed for people who want extra adjustable knee support during everyday movement. That includes walking, stairs, workouts, long work shifts, travel, housework, gardening and physically demanding jobs involving standing, lifting, carrying or bending.

- **Is DialFit suitable for physically demanding work?** It can be used for additional knee support during jobs involving long periods of standing, walking, lifting, carrying, bending or climbing. The dial lets you adjust the tension as the demands of your day change.

- **Can extra body weight make knee support useful?** Extra body weight can make everyday walking and stairs feel more demanding on the knees. DialFit provides adjustable external support that can help the knee feel more secure during movement.

- **Can DialFit be used during pregnancy?** Pregnancy can change body weight and how everyday movement feels. If your healthcare professional says a knee support is appropriate for you, DialFit provides adjustable external support for walking and daily activity.

- **What if it doesn't work for me?** You're covered by our 30-Day Money-Back Guarantee. Try DialFit during your normal routine and contact us within the guarantee period if it isn't right for you.

